              <p><strong>Email:</strong> swordparkour@gmail.com, <strong>Phone:</strong> +63 963 876 6570, <strong>Address:</strong> Manila, Philippines</p>
          </section>

          <hr>

          <section class="faq-section">
            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
              <div class="faq-item">
                  <p class="question">Q: What categories are covered in the quiz?</p>
                  <p class="answer">A: The quiz includes a wide range of topics such as Land Vehicles (cars and motorcycles), Aircrafts, Watercrafts, and the general history of transportation.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="faq-item">
                  <p class="question">Q: Do I need to create an account to take the quiz?</p>
                  <p class="answer">A: No, you can start the quiz immediately as a guest. However, creating an account may allow you to track your high scores in the future.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="faq-item">
                  <p class="question">Q: Can I retake the quiz if I fail?</p>
                  <p class="answer">A: Definitely! You can retake the quiz as many times as you like to improve your score and learn more about different vehicles.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="faq-item">
                  <p class="question">Q: Is the quiz mobile-friendly?</p>
                  <p class="answer">A: Yes, our portal is designed to be fully responsive, meaning you can enjoy the trivia on your smartphone, tablet, or desktop.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="faq-item">
                  <p class="question">Q: How are the scores calculated?</p>
                  <p class="answer">A: Scores are usually based on the number of correct answers. Some advanced levels may also factor in how quickly you complete the quiz!</p>
              </div>
          </section>

          <hr>

          <section class="social-media">
              <h2>Follow Us</h2>
              <div class="social-links">
                  <a href="#" class="social-btn facebook">Facebook</a>
                  <a href="#" class="social-btn twitter">Twitter</a>
                  <a href="#" class="social-btn instagram">Instagram</a>
              </div>
          </section>

          <p>
            Visit the <a href="/start">Start</a> page to learn how it integrates
            with OpenTDB.
          </p>
